  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Among the various types of gardens, describe five gardens briefly.', '1. Formal garden - symmetrical layout with geometric beds, straight paths, clipped hedges and topiary (e.g. French gardens). 2. Informal/English landscape garden - natural curves, rolling lawns, groups of trees, lakes, imitating nature. 3. Japanese/Zen garden - minimalist, asymmetrical, with rocks, raked gravel, water, moss and pruned trees for contemplation. 4. Rock garden - rocks and alpine or succulent plants on slopes; suits Bhutan''s hilly terrain. 5. Xeriscape garden - drought-tolerant plants and mulch needing little water. Others: herb/kitchen garden, rose garden, water garden with ponds and aquatic plants, cottage garden, vertical/roof gardens in towns.', null, '[{"point": "Five garden types described (1 each): formal, informal/ English landscape, Japanese/ Zen, rock garden, xeriscape, herb/ kitchen, rose garden, cottage, water garden, terrace/ vertical/ roof garden, monastery/ Bhutanese courtyard garden", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
