  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case I: Landscaping for Gelephu Mindfulness City
Every Bhutanese is aware of the upcoming developments in Gelephu Mindfulness City (GMC). In developed countries, landscaping and beautification are integral to urban planning and environmental management.

2. In your opinion, how would Gelephu Mindfulness City (GMC) contribute to the growth of the floral industry? (20 marks)', 'GMC will create large, steady demand for ornamental plants and flowers: landscaping of parks, streets, campuses and residential areas; hotels, resorts, wellness centres, offices, events and conferences; and residents and tourists buying flowers for homes, offerings and gifts. Gelephu''s warm subtropical climate suits tropical flowers, orchids, foliage plants and year-round production, encouraging commercial nurseries and greenhouses nearby and reducing imports from India. GMC''s investment-friendly policies, logistics hub and planned airport could attract foreign investment, modern greenhouse technology and export of high-value flowers and plants to regional markets. It would create businesses and jobs - landscaping firms, florists, nursery workers and designers - especially for youth, with training and research links. Branding linked to mindfulness, sustainability and Bhutan''s natural beauty would add value. Farmers in Sarpang and neighbouring dzongkhags could supply through contract farming and cooperatives, building a full value chain (planting material, inputs, cold chain, packaging).', null, '[{"point": "Demand: large-scale landscaping, parks, streets, hotels, events, residents, tourism, corporate/ hospitality sector", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Production/ supply: commercial nurseries, greenhouses in warm southern climate, tropical flowers/ orchids, import substitution, export via GMC logistics/ airport", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Jobs/ enterprises: landscaping firms, florists, youth employment, training, value chain (seeds, bulbs, potting, cold chain)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Investment/ policy: FDI, technology, research, branding (mindfulness, sustainability), linkages with farmers", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'beautification-officer'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 20,
    2160, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (Technical, Beautification Officer): BCSE 2024 - check flagged answer keys before publishing", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2024 Main Examination, Technical Paper III, Beautification Officer", "year": 2024, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/technical-paper-iii/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-technical-3-beauty2024-case1', 2, null, null, (select id from public.specialisations where code = 'beautification-officer'), null)
