  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case II: The Royal Bhutan Flower Exhibition
The Royal Bhutan Flower Exhibition (RBFE) is an annual event organised by the Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock. The first RBFE, held in 2016, reportedly cost over Nu. 20 million. The Ministry plans to resume the event next year.

1. Why do you think organising the RBFE is important? (15 marks)', 'The RBFE promotes floriculture and horticulture as a source of income and jobs, showcasing Bhutan''s rich flora, local growers and new techniques; it encourages citizens, schools and institutions to grow flowers and beautify homes and towns; it attracts domestic and international visitors, supporting tourism and Bhutan''s image as a green, beautiful country; it celebrates royal occasions and national pride and connects to cultural and Buddhist values of flower offerings; it brings knowledge exchange, training, competitions and market linkages for growers and florists; and it develops lasting infrastructure (parks, gardens) and boosts the local economy of the host dzongkhag.', null, '[{"point": "Promotes floriculture/ horticulture as livelihood, showcases Bhutan''s flora/ innovation", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Tourism and national image, celebrating royal occasions/ national pride, cultural values (flowers in Buddhist practice)", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Knowledge sharing, training, market linkages, inspiring citizens/ youth, beautification culture", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Boost local economy of host dzongkhag (infrastructure, business)", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'beautification-officer'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 15,
